) -> Some(0) -> Some(2) -> None -> Some(0) -> Some(3) -> Some(0) ->"},{"DocComment":" Some(4) -> ..."},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" In case `separator` does not implement [`Clone`] or needs to be"},{"DocComment":" computed every time, use [`intersperse_with`]."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Examples"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Basic usage:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" #![feature(iter_intersperse)]"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" let mut a = [0, 1, 2].into_iter().intersperse(100);"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(a.next(), Some(0));   // The first element from `a`."},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(a.next(), Some(100)); // The separator."},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(a.next(), Some(1));   // The next element from `a`."},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(a.next(), Some(100)); // The separator."},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(a.next(), Some(2));   // The last element from `a`."},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(a.next(), None);       // The iterator is finished."},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" `intersperse` can be very useful to join an iterator's items using a common element:"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" #![feature(iter_intersperse)]"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" let words = [\"Hello\", \"World\", \"!\"];"},{"DocComment":" let hello: String = words.into_iter().intersperse(\" \").collect();"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(hello, \"Hello World !\");"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" [`Clone`]: crate::clone::Clone"},{"DocComment":" [`intersperse`]: Iterator::intersperse"},{"DocComment":" [`intersperse_with`]: Iterator::intersperse_with"}],"inline":"Hint","rename":null,"public":true},"is_local":false,"opacity":"Transparent","lang_item":null},"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"index":0,"name":"Self"},{"index":1,"name":"Clause0_Item"}],"const_generics":[],"trait_clauses":[{"clause_id":0,"span":{"data":{"file_id":14,"beg":{"line":1,"col":0},"end":{"line":1,"col":