ine":880,"col":29}},"generated_from_span":null},"source_text":null,"attr_info":{"attributes":[{"DocComment":" Calls a closure on each element of an iterator."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" This is equivalent to using a [`for`] loop on the iterator, although"},{"DocComment":" `break` and `continue` are not possible from a closure. It's generally"},{"DocComment":" more idiomatic to use a `for` loop, but `for_each` may be more legible"},{"DocComment":" when processing items at the end of longer iterator chains. In some"},{"DocComment":" cases `for_each` may also be faster than a loop, because it will use"},{"DocComment":" internal iteration on adapters like `Chain`."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" [`for`]: ../../book/ch03-05-control-flow.html#looping-through-a-collection-with-for"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Examples"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Basic usage:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" use std::sync::mpsc::channel;"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" let (tx, rx) = channel();"},{"DocComment":" (0..5).map(|x| x * 2 + 1)"},{"DocComment":"       .for_each(move |x| tx.send(x).unwrap());"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" let v: Vec<_> = rx.iter().collect();"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(v, vec![1, 3, 5, 7, 9]);"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" For such a small example, a `for` loop may be cleaner, but `for_each`"},{"DocComment":" might be preferable to keep a functional style with longer iterators:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" (0..5).flat_map(|x| (x * 100)..(x * 110))"},{"DocComment":"       .enumerate()"},{"DocComment":"       .filter(|&(i, x)| (i + x) % 3 == 0)"},{"DocComment":"       .for_each(|(i, x)| println!(\"{i}:{x}\"));"},{"DocComment":" ```"}],"inline":"Hint","rename":null,"public":true},"is_local":false,"opacity":"Transparent","lang_item":null},"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"index":0,"name":"Self"},{"index":1,"name":"F"},{"index":2,"name":"Clause0_It