the accumulator will have on the first"},{"DocComment":" call. If applying the closure succeeded against every element of the"},{"DocComment":" iterator, `try_fold()` returns the final accumulator as success."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Folding is useful whenever you have a collection of something, and want"},{"DocComment":" to produce a single value from it."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Note to Implementors"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Several of the other (forward) methods have default implementations in"},{"DocComment":" terms of this one, so try to implement this explicitly if it can"},{"DocComment":" do something better than the default `for` loop implementation."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" In particular, try to have this call `try_fold()` on the internal parts"},{"DocComment":" from which this iterator is composed. If multiple calls are needed,"},{"DocComment":" the `?` operator may be convenient for chaining the accumulator value"},{"DocComment":" along, but beware any invariants that need to be upheld before those"},{"DocComment":" early returns. This is a `&mut self` method, so iteration needs to be"},{"DocComment":" resumable after hitting an error here."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Examples"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Basic usage:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" let a = [1, 2, 3];"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" // the checked sum of all of the elements of the array"},{"DocComment":" let sum = a.into_iter().try_fold(0i8, |acc, x| acc.checked_add(x));"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(sum, Some(6));"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Short-circuiting:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" let a = [10, 20, 30, 100, 40, 50];"},{"DocComment":" let mut iter = a.into_iter();"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" // This sum overflows when adding the 100 element"},{"DocComment":" let sum = iter.try_fold(0i8, |acc, x| acc.checked_add(x));"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(sum, None);"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" // Because it short-circuited, the remaining elements are still"},{"DocComment":" // available through the iterator."},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(iter.len(), 2);"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(iter.next(), Some(40));"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" While you cannot `break` from a closure, the [`ControlFlow`] type allows"},{"DocComment":" a similar idea:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" use std::ops::ControlFlow;"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" let triangular = (1..30).try_fold(0_i8, |prev, x| {"},{"DocComment":"     if let Some(next) = prev.checked_add(x) {"},{"DocComment":"         ControlFlow::Continue(next)"},{"DocComment":"     } else {"},{"DocComment":"         ControlFlow::Break(prev)"},{"DocComment":"     }"},{"DocComment":" });"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(triangular, ControlFlow::Break(120));"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" let triangular = (1..30).try_fold(0_u64, |prev, x| {"},{"DocComment":"     if let Some(next) = prev.checked_add(x) {"},{"DocComment":"         ControlFlow::Continue(next)"},{"DocComment":"     } else {"},{"DocComment":"         ControlFlow::Break(prev)"},{"DocComment":"     }"},{"DocComment":" });"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(triangular, ControlFlow::Continue(435));"},{"DocComment":" ```"}],"inline":"Hint","rename":null,"public":true},"is_local":false,"opacity":"Transparent","lang_item":null},"generics":{"regions":[{"index":0,"name":null,"mutability":"Unknown"}],"types":[{"index":0,"name":"Self"},{"index":1,"name":"B"},{"index":2,"name":"F"},{"index":3,"name":"R"},{"index":4,"name":"Clause0_Item"}],"const_generics":[],"trait_clauses":[{"clause_id":0,"span":{"data":{"file_id":14,"beg":{"line":1,"col":0},"end":{"line":1,"col":0}},"generated_from_span":null},"origin":"TraitSelf","trait_":{"regions":[],"skip_binder":{"id":1,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Deduplicated":31034},{"Deduplicated":31048}]