":" `rposition()` takes a closure that returns `true` or `false`. It applies"},{"DocComment":" this closure to each element of the iterator, starting from the end,"},{"DocComment":" and if one of them returns `true`, then `rposition()` returns"},{"DocComment":" [`Some(index)`]. If all of them return `false`, it returns [`None`]."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" `rposition()` is short-circuiting; in other words, it will stop"},{"DocComment":" processing as soon as it finds a `true`."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" [`Some(index)`]: Some"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Examples"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Basic usage:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" let a = [1, 2, 3];"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(a.into_iter().rposition(|x| x == 3), Some(2));"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(a.into_iter().rposition(|x| x == 5), None);"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Stopping at the first `true`:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" let a = [-1, 2, 3, 4];"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" let mut iter = a.into_iter();"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(iter.rposition(|x| x >= 2), Some(3));"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" // we can still use `iter`, as there are more elements."},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(iter.next(), Some(-1));"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(iter.next_back(), Some(3));"},{"DocComment":" ```"}],"inline":"Hint","rename":null,"public":true},"is_local":false,"opacity":"Transparent","lang_item":null},"generics":{"regions":[{"index":0,"name":null,"mutability":"Unknown"}],"types":[{"index":0,"name":"Self"},{"index":1,"name":"P"},{"index":2,"name":"Clause0_Item"},{"index":3,"name":"Clause2_Clause0_Item"},{"index":4,"name":"Clause3_Clause0_Item"}],"const_generics":[],"trait_clauses":[{"clause_id":0,"span":{"data":{"file_id":14,"beg":{"line":1,"col":0},"end":{"line":1,"col":0}},"generated_from_span":null},"origin":"TraitSelf","trait_":{"reg